//! `ui-devtools`: the devtools window for a running Silk UI. It shows the app's element tree,
//! the selected node's styles and box model, the event log and the frame stats, and highlights
//! the selected node in the app's window. See the README.
//!
//!   ui-devtools [--connect ADDRESS]
//!
//! ADDRESS is in the syntax of `SILK_UI_INSPECT` (`1`, `tcp:<port>` or a socket path) and names
//! the app to inspect, which must be a debug build started with `SILK_UI_INSPECT` set. Without
//! `--connect` it is `1`: the socket `silk-ui-inspect.sock` in the working directory. The app
//! may start after the window; the status line says when it cannot be reached.
//!
//! It keeps one protocol 3 session with the app: a pump thread reads what the app pushes and
//! wakes the window, which then sends the devtools [`Message.Pull`]. The batches of an extension
//! panel's view go to the window instead ([`Relay`]), which replays them in its tree, and the
//! records of their nodes go back to the app (`ui_devtools.remote`).
//!
//! The devtools are a ui-app app themselves, so a debug build of this window serves the
//! inspector too when its own `SILK_UI_INSPECT` is set (to another address than the app's).
